  "tactics": {
    "styleTags": [
      "Defensive Solidity",
      "Physical",
      "Counter-Attack",
      "Hard to Beat"
    ],
    "tacticalNote": "Alfaro organizes Paraguay in a deep 4-2-3-1 with two holding midfielders sitting narrowly in front of the back four, eliminating central spaces. They defend in two disciplined banks before launching rapid counter-attacks through Almirón's movement on the right and Enciso's creativity centrally. Set pieces — both offensive and defensive — are meticulously prepared and represent their most reliable route to goals against elite opposition.",
    "strength": "Defensive compactness that suffocates space — even top-10 sides have historically found it extremely difficult to break down a well-organized Paraguay.",
    "vulnerability": "Sustained possession pressure from multiple angles can stretch the defensive structure, and when forced to chase a deficit they lack the individual quality to dominate open games."
  },
  "watchFor": [
    "Enciso's movement between the lines — when he finds pockets behind the USA midfield, Paraguay are at their most dangerous",
